hackrfduplex (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * One shared time for both streams, from a calibration burst or a
    trigger edge, and timed transmit and receive to the sample.
  * Faults reported as stream statuses: lost samples, a stopped or
    unplugged board, a lost time origin; the transmitter stops by itself
    if its host stops feeding it.
  * The rest of the SoapySDR contract: clock and time sources, the
    lo_locked, ref_locked and time_locked sensors, direct buffer access,
    sample rates refused outside their range, unsupported calls refused.
  * A receive ring sized to the sample rate; the device opens at the
    boards' own 10 Msps.
  * Optional receive DC removal and I/Q balance correction (liquid-dsp).
  * hackrfduplex-check: timed bursts, recovery, the acceptance battery,
    and a man page.

 -- Tom Cully <mail@tomcully.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:35:42 +0000

